understand the difference between the ledger and the ATM.

10:04.360 --> 10:08.160
So if accountants understand this, why don't physicists?

10:08.780 --> 10:13.360
Why do the physics community suddenly demand that their internal ledger only have positive

10:13.360 --> 10:13.760
numbers?

10:14.080 --> 10:17.680
Well, here is the incredible irony that Flickshina highlights in the paper.

10:17.680 --> 10:23.060
However, physicists actually do understand this, and they already use larger state spaces with

10:23.060 --> 10:25.060
negative numbers in other areas of physics.

10:25.580 --> 10:30.800
They just developed a bizarre, highly specific amnesia when it came to gravity.

10:31.020 --> 10:31.400
Wait, really?

