13:27.720 --> 13:30.200
It just makes the math agonizingly difficult.

13:30.820 --> 13:34.060
But with gravity, the ghost wasn't just a bookkeeping trick.

13:34.060 --> 13:38.220
The ghost was fundamentally baked into the dynamics of the theory itself.

13:38.740 --> 13:39.780
And that terrified them.

13:40.020 --> 13:42.560
This brings us to the Great Crisis of 1977.

13:43.280 --> 13:47.620
Let's talk about the discovery that should have changed physics, but instead got thrown in the trash.

13:48.060 --> 13:50.200
Who is K.S. Stel and what did he find?

13:50.320 --> 13:56.620
K.S. Stel was a theoretical physicist who was tackling the biggest problem in modern science, quantum gravity.

13:56.620 --> 14:04.620
The problem with standard Einstein gravity general relativity is that when you try to apply the rules of quantum mechanics to it, the math simply explodes.

14:05.420 --> 14:06.040
It breaks down.

14:06.180 --> 14:06.520
Completely.

14:07.060 --> 14:12.660
When you try to calculate the interaction of gravitons at incredibly small distances, the equations spit out infinities.

14:13.100 --> 14:15.300
Infinite energy, infinite probability.

14:15.840 --> 14:17.840
The theory is what we call non-renormalizable.

14:18.260 --> 14:19.000
It just breaks.

14:19.000 --> 14:21.680
It's like trying to divide by zero on a calculator.

14:22.060 --> 14:23.620
You just get a big error message.

14:24.100 --> 14:24.380
Exactly.

14:24.780 --> 14:27.260
And for decades, physicists tried to fix this and failed.

14:27.840 --> 14:32.300
But in 1977, Stel made a monumental mathematical discovery.

14:33.160 --> 14:39.660
He found that if you modify Einstein's equations, specifically if you add quadratic curvature terms to the action.

14:39.860 --> 14:40.160
Hang on.

14:40.220 --> 14:40.920
Let's define that.

14:41.040 --> 14:42.940
What is a quadratic curvature term?

14:42.940 --> 14:43.300
Sure.

14:43.640 --> 14:49.400
General relativity is based on space-time curvature, represented by the Ricci scalar, which is a linear term.

14:49.840 --> 14:52.020
It's essentially the first derivative of the metric.

14:52.860 --> 14:58.360
Stel decided to add terms that are squared, the square of the Ricci scalar and the square of something called the whale tensor.

14:58.800 --> 15:02.540
He introduced higher order derivatives into the fundamental equations of gravity.

15:02.740 --> 15:04.140
Okay, so he squared some stuff.

15:04.260 --> 15:04.460
Right.

15:04.600 --> 15:09.220
And when he ran the calculations for this new quadratic gravity, a miracle happened.

15:09.420 --> 15:11.340
The equation stopped spinning out infinities.

15:11.340 --> 15:13.860
The theory became perfectly renormalizable.

15:14.100 --> 15:15.700
The infinities were entirely cured.

15:15.900 --> 15:24.280
Okay, so a guy in 1977 completely solved the infinity problem of quantum gravity by just squaring some of the curvature terms.

15:24.440 --> 15:26.140
That sounds like the Holy Grail.

15:26.520 --> 15:28.320
That should be Einstein-level famous.

15:28.700 --> 15:32.200
Why aren't we all taught Stel's quadratic gravity in high school?

15:32.520 --> 15:33.820
Because of the fatal flaw.

15:34.580 --> 15:40.100
When you add those higher derivative terms, you fundamentally change the particle spectrum of the theory.

15:40.100 --> 15:47.140
In standard Einstein gravity, you have the graviton, a massless spin-to particle that carries the gravitational force.

15:47.660 --> 15:53.040
When Stel added the quadratic terms, the math still produced the massless graviton, which was great.

15:53.120 --> 15:53.340
What?

15:53.840 --> 15:55.260
But it also birthed a monster.

15:55.840 --> 15:59.320
It created a massive spin-to propagating degree of freedom.

16:00.020 --> 16:07.300
And when you look at the kinetic energy term for this new massive particle in the equations, it has a massive negative sign in front of it.

16:07.300 --> 16:09.920
The negative kinetic energy, meaning what physically?

16:10.160 --> 16:11.660
Think about a ball rolling down a hill.

16:12.380 --> 16:16.800
Positive kinetic energy means if you push the ball, it speeds up in the direction you pushed it.

16:17.400 --> 16:21.320
A particle with a negative kinetic term, a ghost, behaves inversely.

16:21.420 --> 16:23.620
If you push it forward, it accelerates backward.

16:23.780 --> 16:24.500
It's bizarre.

16:24.500 --> 16:25.040
It is.

16:25.380 --> 16:30.160
If it emits radiation, instead of losing energy and slowing down, it gains energy and speeds up.

16:31.000 --> 16:41.000
Furthermore, when you translate this into quantum mechanics via canonical quantization, this negative kinetic term forces the particle's quantum states to have a negative inner product.

16:41.320 --> 16:43.860
It creates a state with a negative probability.

16:43.860 --> 16:44.360
Yes.

16:45.020 --> 16:48.540
The ghost states represent a negative probability of existence.

16:49.360 --> 17:03.420
So standard physics looked at Stel's brilliant cure for quantum gravity, saw the massive spin-to ghost with its negative probability, invoked the Hilbert assumption, and said negative probability is an observable pathology.

17:03.840 --> 17:07.660
It is unphysical, therefore the entire theory is dead on arrival.

17:07.780 --> 17:08.160
Wow.

17:08.480 --> 17:12.660
And they threw quadratic gravity straight in the theoretical trash can.

17:12.660 --> 17:17.800
They discarded the literal cure for quantum gravity because they couldn't handle the ghost in the ledger.

17:18.100 --> 17:21.880
They just assumed the negative math would inevitably leak into the physical world.

17:22.440 --> 17:31.940
But Flyxion's paper highlights a massive, decades-long rescue operation, right, a way to save stealth theory, spearheaded recently by physicists Neil Turok and Sam Bateman.

17:32.100 --> 17:32.500
That's right.

17:32.760 --> 17:37.880
And their solution involves abandoning the Hilbert space entirely and moving into something called a crane space.

17:38.480 --> 17:41.780
So what is a crane space mathematically, and how does it save the ghost?

17:41.780 --> 17:46.540
A crane space is a mathematical arena that explicitly rejects the Hilbert assumption.

17:47.280 --> 17:49.440
It is an indefinite inner product space.

17:50.100 --> 17:58.900
Unlike a Hilbert space, which violently demands that every single vector have a positive length and a positive probability, a crane space is completely relaxed.

17:59.440 --> 18:05.160
It is perfectly happy to contain a positive norm sector and a negative norm sector simultaneously.

18:05.160 --> 18:07.280
Okay, but how does that actually help?

18:07.340 --> 18:13.400
If you just mathematically allow the negative probability to exist, you haven't solved the physical absurdity.

18:13.480 --> 18:14.860
You still have a negative probability.

18:15.260 --> 18:19.340
To see the mechanics of that, we have to look at Neil Turok's brilliant analogy.

18:20.200 --> 18:24.800
Think of Winkowski spacetime, the geometric foundation of Einstein's special relativity.

18:24.800 --> 18:29.740
In four-dimensional spacetime, we have three dimensions of space and one dimension of time.

18:30.300 --> 18:32.580
And crucially, they are mathematically distinct.

18:33.300 --> 18:35.640
Spacelike vectors have a positive length squared.

18:36.360 --> 18:38.540
Timelike vectors have a negative length squared.

18:38.760 --> 18:39.340
Oh, interesting.

18:39.540 --> 18:43.540
So the geometry of the universe actually already uses indefinite metrics.

18:43.540 --> 18:44.380
Exactly.

18:45.100 --> 18:47.860
Spacetime itself is an indefinite metric space.

18:48.460 --> 18:52.600
Spacetime isn't broken just because the time direction has a negative sign in the metric.

18:53.140 --> 18:55.560
It just means time behaves differently than space.

18:56.360 --> 19:01.000
Turok and Bateman apply that exact same logic to the quantum state space.

19:01.160 --> 19:02.240
So they treat it like geometry.

19:02.700 --> 19:02.940
Yes.

19:03.460 --> 19:08.360
A crane space is just a quantum algebra that acknowledges time-like and space-like quantum states.

19:08.780 --> 19:11.060
The positive norm states are standard particles.

19:11.180 --> 19:13.440
The negative norm states are the ghosts.

19:14.300 --> 19:19.160
And they are both perfectly valid, well-behaved coordinates internally in the mathematical space.

19:19.280 --> 19:21.080
But I'm still stuck on the ATM analogy.

19:21.520 --> 19:24.780
The accountant can use the negative numbers in the Crean space ledger.

19:25.300 --> 19:30.920
But eventually, the physicist has to calculate an observable physical event like two particles colliding in a collider.

19:31.340 --> 19:32.320
They have to go to the ATM.

19:33.440 --> 19:38.860
If your equation spits out a negative probability state, a ghost, how does the universe just ignore it?

19:38.860 --> 19:42.640
How do you get a positive, sensible physical probability out of a Crean space?

19:42.640 --> 19:45.900
This is the crux of the entire rescue operation.

19:46.880 --> 19:51.660
This is what Flyxion formalizes as the observable admissibility theorem.

19:53.180 --> 20:00.440
Turok and Bateman realized that the physicists in the 1970s were calculating probabilities entirely wrong.

20:00.580 --> 20:01.260
Oh, so.

20:01.260 --> 20:04.300
In standard quantum mechanics, you use the Born rule.

20:04.720 --> 20:10.300
You take the amplitude of a state and you square it, and you basically ignore anything that doesn't physically exist.

20:10.920 --> 20:15.580
The 70s physicists tried to just delete the ghost states from the math before doing the calculation,

20:16.120 --> 20:19.600
trying to artificially force the Crean space back into a Hilbert space.

20:19.600 --> 20:24.120
But when you just arbitrarily delete a mathematically necessary part of the equation,

20:24.380 --> 20:28.820
you break the theory's internal symmetries, and the probabilities stop adding up to 100%.

20:28.820 --> 20:30.760
It ruins the unitarity of the theory.

20:30.880 --> 20:34.060
So you can't just cross the negative numbers out of the ledger with a Sharpie.

20:34.140 --> 20:35.680
The books literally won't balance.

20:35.780 --> 20:36.000
Right.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.360
So Turok and Bateman modified the approach.

20:38.520 --> 20:39.660
They said, leave the ghosts in.

20:40.040 --> 20:41.360
Trace over the entire space.

20:41.360 --> 20:43.540
But, and this is the genius part,

20:43.940 --> 20:48.840
they identified a hidden mathematical symmetry in quadratic gravity called ghost parity symmetry.

20:49.200 --> 20:50.440
Ghost parity symmetry.

20:51.340 --> 20:53.180
Okay, let's break down the mechanics of that.

20:53.260 --> 20:53.960
How does it work?

20:54.240 --> 20:56.420
Imagine a perfectly balanced equation,

20:56.820 --> 21:02.340
where every time a regular positive energy particle interacts and moves forward in time,

21:02.340 --> 21:08.100
its negative ghost counterpart mirrors that mathematical action perfectly in the background.

21:08.100 --> 21:12.680
Because they are locked in this perfectly symmetrical dance under the rules of the theory,

21:13.240 --> 21:17.020
a positive state can never spontaneously mix with a negative state.

21:17.820 --> 21:23.660
The symmetry acts as an impenetrable firewall between the positive norm sector and the negative norm sector.

21:24.060 --> 21:26.600
So they exist in the exact same mathematical universe,

21:26.740 --> 21:30.180
but they can never physically touch or convert into one another.

21:30.320 --> 21:30.700
Exactly.

21:31.260 --> 21:34.640
The time evolution of the system strictly commutes with this parity operator.

21:34.640 --> 21:41.100
And because of this firewall, the observable admissibility theorem proves a stunning mathematical fact.

21:42.200 --> 21:45.340
If you calculate the transition probability of a physical event,

21:45.660 --> 21:47.900
and you leave the ghosts fully engaged in the math,

21:48.160 --> 21:52.940
the negative contributions of the ghosts will always perfectly cancel out any mathematical anomalies,

21:53.240 --> 21:56.240
and the final observable probability will always be positive.

21:56.780 --> 21:57.700
Wait, really?

21:57.920 --> 22:01.640
And it will always sum up perfectly to unity 100%.

22:01.640 --> 22:02.700
That is beautiful.

22:02.700 --> 22:04.980
The math processes the negative ghost,

22:05.420 --> 22:09.200
uses it to carry the necessary information to cancel out the infinities of gravity,

22:09.560 --> 22:11.660
but because of the ghost parity firewall,

22:12.280 --> 22:15.200
by the time the calculation reaches the observable output,

22:15.600 --> 22:18.020
the negativity has perfectly washed itself out.

22:18.240 --> 22:18.540
Yes.

22:18.900 --> 22:22.720
And this requires us to deeply internalize the difference between

22:22.720 --> 22:27.540
what Flyxion calls a coordinate pathology and an observable pathology.

22:27.540 --> 22:30.800
A coordinate pathology is a glitch, a weird feature,

22:31.020 --> 22:33.780
or a negative sign in the internal mathematical map.

22:33.940 --> 22:34.680
Like the ledger.

22:34.820 --> 22:35.460
Like the ledger.

22:35.780 --> 22:38.780
An observable pathology is when the physical universe actually breaks

22:38.780 --> 22:41.240
like a negative probability of an event happening in a lab.

22:41.880 --> 22:46.560
Flyxion argues, conclusively, that a ghost is merely a coordinate pathology.

22:46.960 --> 22:50.200
It is a hidden mathematical direction in the admissibility manifold.

22:50.780 --> 22:52.240
It does the heavy lifting in the background,

22:52.560 --> 22:54.680
but it never bleeds into physical reality.

22:54.680 --> 22:59.560
So the physicists in the 1970s threw away the literal cure for quantum gravity

22:59.560 --> 23:03.460
because they confused a coordinate glitch for an observable catastrophe.

23:03.860 --> 23:06.340
They looked at a negative number in the internal ledger

23:06.340 --> 23:09.080
and assumed the ATM was going to start spitting out antimatter.

23:09.580 --> 23:11.860
They mistook the map for the territory.

23:12.180 --> 23:14.500
That is the exact argument this paper is making.

23:15.040 --> 23:17.280
The ghost was never a threat to reality.

23:17.700 --> 23:19.840
It was just a feature of the internal math.

23:19.920 --> 23:21.560
Okay, the math checks out for probabilities.

23:21.760 --> 23:22.560
We solved the ghost.

23:22.560 --> 23:25.880
But if I'm tracking the history of physics correctly,

23:26.480 --> 23:29.420
negative probabilities aren't the only mathematical monster

23:29.420 --> 23:31.280
hiding in these higher derivative theories.

23:31.840 --> 23:33.880
Probabilities are just one part of the equation.

23:34.380 --> 23:35.260
What about energy?

23:35.880 --> 23:39.160
Because there is an older, much scarier mathematical theorem

23:39.160 --> 23:41.240
from way back in the 19th century that says

23:41.240 --> 23:44.820
adding these squared derivatives won't just mess up your probabilities.

23:44.820 --> 23:48.440
It will literally rip the universe apart with infinite energy.

23:48.440 --> 23:51.560
Ah, yes, the Ostrogradsky instability.

23:51.880 --> 23:54.440
It is the great phantom menace of theoretical physics.

23:55.340 --> 24:00.160
It has been used as a club to beat down higher derivative theories for almost 200 years.

24:00.560 --> 24:01.600
Let's set the stage here.

24:02.260 --> 24:07.380
Who was Ostrogradsky and what mathematical curse did he unleash in 1850?

24:07.860 --> 24:10.860
Mikhail Ostrogradsky was a brilliant Russian mathematician.

24:10.860 --> 24:17.260
In 1850, he proved a highly robust, mathematically unassailable theorem in classical mechanics.

24:17.720 --> 24:22.880
He showed that any physical system whose equations rely on irreducible higher-order derivatives,

24:23.120 --> 24:28.260
meaning derivatives higher than the first order, like acceleration or the quadratic terms

24:28.260 --> 24:33.260
in Stel's gravity, will inherently possess a Hamiltonian that is unbounded below.

24:33.260 --> 24:34.280
Okay, let's unpack that.

24:34.380 --> 24:34.960
The Hamiltonian.

24:35.060 --> 24:40.700
In physics, the Hamiltonian is essentially the master equation for the total energy of a system, correct?

24:40.980 --> 24:41.380
Exactly.

24:41.640 --> 24:42.920
It represents the total energy.

24:43.260 --> 24:48.060
In a normal, healthy, physical system, the Hamiltonian has a floor, a ground state.

24:48.140 --> 24:51.660
The energy can't go to low zero or at least below some minimum value.

24:52.060 --> 24:54.780
But Ostrogradsky proved that if your equations have higher derivatives,

24:55.100 --> 24:58.740
the momentum of the system becomes linearly dependent on those higher derivatives.

24:58.740 --> 25:03.220
And because it's a linear dependence, you can push the energy arbitrarily far into the negative.

25:03.360 --> 25:04.380
There is no bottom floor.

25:04.580 --> 25:06.320
The Hamiltonian is unbounded below.

25:06.880 --> 25:09.600
It can plunge infinitely toward negative infinity.

25:09.820 --> 25:14.480
And what is the actual physical consequence of an energy state with no bottom floor?

25:14.680 --> 25:15.940
Well, in isolation, nothing.

25:16.500 --> 25:17.960
But the universe isn't isolated.

25:18.440 --> 25:19.220
Things interact.

25:19.760 --> 25:22.100
The standard physics interpretation is catastrophic.

25:22.800 --> 25:27.280
If you take a normal system, say, standard electromagnetic fields with positive energy,

25:27.280 --> 25:31.420
and you couple it to an Ostrogradsky system like higher derivative gravity,

25:32.060 --> 25:34.500
you get a runaway infinite energy exchange.

25:34.700 --> 25:35.320
Like a cascade.

25:35.500 --> 25:36.760
A catastrophic cascade.

25:37.020 --> 25:37.200
Yeah.

25:37.280 --> 25:39.860
Because the Ostrogradsky system has no bottom floor,

25:40.080 --> 25:42.540
it can drop infinitely downward into negative energy.

25:42.780 --> 25:47.140
And because of the strict conservation of total energy for every unit of negative energy it drops,

25:47.500 --> 25:51.060
it pumps a unit of positive infinite energy into the normal system.

25:51.420 --> 25:54.340
The higher derivative system plunges to negative infinity,

25:54.340 --> 25:56.640
the normal system shoots up to positive infinity,

25:56.920 --> 26:02.000
and the universe instantly vaporizes in a runaway explosion of infinite heat and radiation.

26:02.380 --> 26:03.760
Well, I mean, I don't know about you,

26:03.800 --> 26:08.800
but I feel like I would have noticed if the universe had vaporized in a cascade of infinite energy.

26:09.240 --> 26:11.580
That definitely sounds like an observable pathology.

26:11.940 --> 26:16.360
You can't just sweep infinite explosive energy under the rug with a clever probability trick.

26:16.360 --> 26:22.600
So how on earth does Flyxion's framework survive 170-year-old mathematical proof

26:22.600 --> 26:25.040
that their theory should instantly destroy the universe?

26:25.560 --> 26:32.400
You survive it by applying the exact same coordinate versus observable lens that we just used for the ghosts.

26:32.680 --> 26:39.120
You have to look at what Ostrogradsky actually proved versus what physicists merely assumed he proved.

26:39.760 --> 26:43.100
Flyxion explains this through a concept he calls the trajectory shift.

26:43.280 --> 26:44.780
What's the trajectory shift?

26:44.780 --> 26:48.900
You see, Ostrogradsky made a mathematical claim about the phase space of the system.

26:49.580 --> 26:52.980
Phase space is the vast, multidimensional mathematical arena

26:52.980 --> 26:56.200
of all potentially possible states a system could occupy,

26:56.580 --> 26:58.340
regardless of the actual laws of motion.

26:58.880 --> 27:02.100
But observable physics isn't about the whole phase space.

27:02.460 --> 27:06.260
It is about the actual histories or trajectories that the dynamics generate over time,

27:06.580 --> 27:08.220
based on actual initial conditions.

27:08.380 --> 27:10.800
I'm going to need a strong analogy to visualize this.

27:10.800 --> 27:14.080
I'm thinking about a roller coaster.

27:14.280 --> 27:18.940
Let's say Ostrogradsky is a hyper-pedantic safety inspector

27:18.940 --> 27:23.880
looking at a mathematical blueprint of a completely wild new roller coaster.

27:24.000 --> 27:24.680
Okay, I'm waiting.

27:24.740 --> 27:27.120
And he points the equations of the blueprint and says,

27:27.600 --> 27:29.320
look, according to this math,

27:29.400 --> 27:33.200
the track technically extends infinitely down into the bedrock of the earth.

27:33.200 --> 27:35.320
It's an unbounded phase space.

27:35.840 --> 27:39.420
The cart has the mathematical potential to plunge to the center of the planet.

27:39.640 --> 27:44.060
But as the person actually strapped into the cart riding the roller coaster,

27:44.200 --> 27:47.320
I'm sitting there saying it doesn't matter where the theoretical blueprint could go.

27:47.660 --> 27:51.040
The actual physical cart is locked onto a specific dynamic loop.

27:51.420 --> 27:55.500
The laws of momentum and the track design strictly dictate its trajectory.

27:55.500 --> 27:58.560
It never actually accesses those downward infinite tracks.

27:58.720 --> 27:59.960
Is that the trajectory shift?

27:59.960 --> 28:02.680
That is a phenomenal, perfect analogy.

28:03.460 --> 28:07.260
The person riding the coaster represents the physical observable trajectory.

28:07.900 --> 28:11.680
Ostrogradsky is panicking about the empty mathematically possible space

28:11.680 --> 28:14.140
beneath the tracks that the cart never actually reaches.

28:15.040 --> 28:18.080
The phase space has a runaway direction mathematically,

28:18.560 --> 28:21.720
but the actual dynamic trajectory is completely stable.

28:21.900 --> 28:22.960
An analogy is great,

28:23.100 --> 28:27.020
but do we have proof that physical systems actually behave this way?

28:27.020 --> 28:31.300
That they can have an unbounded phase space, but a perfectly stable trajectory.

28:31.580 --> 28:32.300
You absolutely do.

28:32.560 --> 28:36.940
The paper highlights a classic physics model called the Pius-Ullenbeck oscillator.

28:37.660 --> 28:41.700
It was formulated in 1950 specifically to study this exact problem.

28:42.420 --> 28:46.360
It's a theoretical model of a particle governed by a fourth-order differential equation.

28:46.960 --> 28:48.120
Because it has higher derivatives,

28:48.560 --> 28:51.660
its Hamiltonian is strictly mathematically unbounded below,

28:52.060 --> 28:53.600
exactly as Ostrogradsky warned.

28:54.040 --> 28:55.500
According to the naive interpretation,

28:55.500 --> 28:56.880
it should just explode.

28:57.000 --> 28:57.520
But it doesn't.

28:57.660 --> 28:58.460
It doesn't.

28:58.560 --> 29:02.620
When you actually sit down and calculate the physical motion of the Pius-Ullenbeck oscillator,

29:03.160 --> 29:04.600
when you map the trajectory,

29:05.520 --> 29:08.640
the fourth-order equation beautifully decomposes

29:08.640 --> 29:13.420
into two coupled, standard, second-order harmonic oscillators.

29:13.560 --> 29:14.160
Meaning what?

29:14.420 --> 29:17.540
It literally just becomes two pendulums swinging back and forth.

29:17.540 --> 29:23.000
Its actual physical motion is perfectly bounded, periodic, and eternally stable.

29:23.600 --> 29:24.740
It never explodes.

29:24.740 --> 29:30.160
The runaway infinite energy directions undeniably exist in the mathematical phase space,

29:30.280 --> 29:30.680
the blueprint.

29:31.320 --> 29:33.740
But the physical trajectory never, ever goes there.

29:33.980 --> 29:39.120
So you're saying a 19th century mathematician proved a theorem that terrified physicists for a

29:39.120 --> 29:42.140
century and a half, and it turns out it's mathematically true,

29:42.260 --> 29:45.040
but totally physically irrelevant to the actual outcome.

29:45.280 --> 29:48.460
It is a property of the state space, not a property of the history.

29:48.460 --> 29:53.920
And Neil Turok, when applying this to quadratic gravity, made an even more brilliant observation.

29:54.700 --> 29:57.920
Physicists have been terrified of gravity having a negative energy instability.

29:58.640 --> 30:01.000
But gravity already has negative energy.

30:01.140 --> 30:02.900
It's a fundamental feature of general relativity.

30:03.100 --> 30:04.740
Wait, gravity has negative energy?

30:04.740 --> 30:10.080
Yes, the gravitational potential energy of any bound system, like the Earth orbiting the

30:10.080 --> 30:11.680
Sun, is negative.

30:12.460 --> 30:17.220
You have to add positive energy to the Earth like a massive rocket booster to break it out

30:17.220 --> 30:18.400
of the negative gravity well.

30:18.520 --> 30:21.700
Okay, so negative energy isn't new, but what about the runaway cascade?

30:21.900 --> 30:22.820
That's the scary part.

30:22.820 --> 30:25.060
Look at the observable universe right now.

30:25.420 --> 30:30.640
Observations confirmed in the late 1990s that our universe is undergoing exponential accelerating

30:30.640 --> 30:31.220
expansion.

30:32.060 --> 30:32.760
Dark energy.

30:33.540 --> 30:38.420
Out of context, if you just handed a mathematician the equations for exponential expansion, it

30:38.420 --> 30:40.820
looks exactly like an Ostrogrodsky runaway instability.

30:41.140 --> 30:42.200
Wait, hang on a second.

30:42.360 --> 30:46.420
The expansion of our universe looks mathematically identical to an Ostrogrodsky instability.

30:46.820 --> 30:47.180
Yes.

30:47.720 --> 30:52.800
If you look at the scale factor of the universe growing exponentially, the coordinate spaces

30:52.800 --> 30:53.940
is racing toward infinity.

30:54.860 --> 30:59.340
Turok points out that it sounds awfully like a catastrophic instability, but look out the

30:59.340 --> 30:59.580
window.

31:00.180 --> 31:03.840
It is demonstrably a perfectly stable cosmological solution.

31:04.620 --> 31:07.960
The universe isn't exploding in a cascade of localized infinite heat.

31:08.240 --> 31:09.740
It is just expanding smoothly.

31:10.500 --> 31:16.160
When Turok and Bateman analyzed their four-derivative quadratic gravity theory, they found that the Ostrogrodsky

31:16.160 --> 31:21.880
runaway direction in the extended phase space corresponds precisely to normal, perfectly stable

31:21.880 --> 31:23.820
exponential cosmological expansion.

31:23.820 --> 31:24.940
That is incredible.

31:25.200 --> 31:29.480
So the terrifying mathematical instability that has been the boogeyman of quantum gravity

31:29.480 --> 31:32.640
since the 1850s is just, well, it's just the universe expanding.

31:32.760 --> 31:33.180
Exactly.

31:33.700 --> 31:36.140
The instability is not an observable pathology.

31:36.640 --> 31:41.560
It is simply a coordinate description of ordinary cosmological behavior in the admissibility

31:41.560 --> 31:42.000
manifold.

31:42.580 --> 31:45.700
The blueprint looks scary, but the rollercoaster ride is perfectly smooth.

31:45.700 --> 31:49.940
Okay, if this is true, it forces a massive philosophical pivot.

31:50.940 --> 31:55.560
If negative probabilities, ghosts, and infinite runaway energies can all be safely hidden away

31:55.560 --> 32:00.980
as mathematical shadows in the internal ledger, it forces us to rethink the very mechanism

32:00.980 --> 32:02.860
that casts those shadows in the first place.

32:03.280 --> 32:08.680
If we are only seeing the positive, bounded, stable output, what is the filter?

32:09.060 --> 32:13.000
What is the ATM machine actually doing to the math before we observe it?

32:13.000 --> 32:17.100
Which brings us to arguably the most paradigm-shifting section of Flyxion's paper.

32:17.600 --> 32:20.920
We have to talk about how quantum probability itself is generated.

32:21.320 --> 32:24.820
We have to talk about the squaring trick and the true nature of the Bourne rule.

32:24.980 --> 32:26.360
Yes, section four of the outline.

32:26.620 --> 32:30.160
This is the part of the paper that really blew my mind because it attacks a concept I thought

32:30.160 --> 32:32.260
was a completely foundational axiom of nature.

32:32.800 --> 32:34.060
Let's talk about the Bourne rule.

32:34.320 --> 32:36.960
What is it and how have physicists traditionally viewed it?

32:36.960 --> 32:42.520
The Bourne rule is the fundamental bridge between the bizarre abstract math of quantum mechanics

32:42.520 --> 32:44.240
and the tangible real world.

32:44.880 --> 32:50.340
In quantum math, a system is described by a wave function which assigns a probability amplitude

32:50.340 --> 32:52.160
to every possible outcome.

32:52.520 --> 32:54.400
But these amplitudes are not normal numbers.

32:54.540 --> 32:55.600
They are complex numbers.

32:56.020 --> 33:00.220
They have a real part and an imaginary part involving e, the square root of negative one.

33:00.300 --> 33:01.640
You can't observe an imaginary number.

33:02.160 --> 33:04.560
So in 1926, Max Bourne proposed a rule.

33:04.940 --> 33:08.880
To find the actual observable probability of an event happening in the physical world,

33:08.880 --> 33:13.320
you take that complex quantum amplitude and you square its absolute value.

33:13.480 --> 33:13.960
It's modulus.

33:14.320 --> 33:18.180
The result is a normal positive real number between zero and one, a probability.

33:18.640 --> 33:23.880
And for a century, physicists have treated that rule squaring the amplitude as an irreducible

33:23.880 --> 33:25.960
fundamental law of nature.

33:26.260 --> 33:28.040
It's just what the universe does.

33:28.700 --> 33:31.300
But Flyxion's paper argues it is not fundamental.

33:31.580 --> 33:36.280
It argues the Bourne rule is a derived quantity, a coarse graining theorem.

33:36.280 --> 33:37.200
It's a filter.

33:38.000 --> 33:38.960
Okay, let's break this down.

33:39.280 --> 33:43.100
The paper introduces Tristan Needham's geometric view of complex numbers.

33:43.600 --> 33:48.420
Now, I always learned in high school math that an imaginary number, it was just a mathematical

33:48.420 --> 33:52.420
trick, a placeholder, because you can't actually take the square root of a negative number.

33:52.800 --> 33:55.380
But Needham says it's not just a quantity, it's an action.

33:55.800 --> 33:56.360
What does that mean?

33:56.900 --> 34:00.920
Tristan Needham wrote a seminal, beautiful book called Visual Complex Analysis.

34:01.240 --> 34:03.920
His core argument is that we teach complex numbers terribly.

34:03.920 --> 34:07.540
A complex number is not just a point on a two-dimensional graph.

34:07.660 --> 34:08.580
It is an operation.

34:09.000 --> 34:10.640
It's an active geometric command.

34:10.860 --> 34:14.860
When you multiply something by a complex number, you are doing two things simultaneously.

34:15.380 --> 34:20.000
You are scaling its magnitude stretching or shrinking it, and you are rotating it by

34:20.000 --> 34:21.580
a specific angle of phase.

34:21.740 --> 34:23.900
So the imaginary unit isn't just a fake number.

34:24.300 --> 34:24.540
No.

34:24.980 --> 34:30.900
The imaginary unit I is literally a geometric command to execute a quarter turn, a 90-degree

34:30.900 --> 34:32.640
rotation in the mathematical space.

34:33.280 --> 34:35.760
A complex number is a packet of instructions.

34:36.480 --> 34:39.720
Stretch the vector by this much, and rotate it by this angle.

34:39.720 --> 34:45.600
Okay, so the quantum state inside the admissibility manifold is full of these complex numbers, meaning

34:45.600 --> 34:49.520
it's full of dynamic geometric constructions, phases, rotations, twistings.

34:50.240 --> 34:53.900
What happens when you apply the Born rule to that geometry?

34:53.900 --> 34:57.540
What actually happens when you mathematically take the modulus squared?

34:58.120 --> 35:01.760
Mathematically, when you take the modulus squared of a complex number, you are extracting

35:01.760 --> 35:06.380
the length of the vector, squaring it, and crucially, you are entirely discarding the

35:06.380 --> 35:06.660
angle.

35:06.820 --> 35:09.280
You are completely throwing away the rotation, the phase.

35:09.380 --> 35:12.020
You are literally deleting geometric data from the unit.

35:12.040 --> 35:13.220
You are deleting the geometry.

35:13.920 --> 35:16.140
The Born rule is not a fundamental act of creation.

35:16.560 --> 35:19.020
It is an operation of discarding geometric information.

35:19.020 --> 35:24.200
This connects to a deeply rigorous framework developed by Harvard physicist Jacob Brandes

35:24.200 --> 35:28.880
called the RSVP framework and the mathematics of in the stochastic matrices.

35:29.400 --> 35:31.120
Let's dig into the RSVP framework.

35:31.440 --> 35:32.440
What is coarse graining?

35:32.680 --> 35:37.940
Without getting bogged down in the impenetrable equations, coarse graining is a concept from statistical

35:37.940 --> 35:38.480
mechanics.

35:39.260 --> 35:40.660
Think about a box of gas.

35:41.100 --> 35:46.860
You could mathematically track the exact position and velocity of all 10 trillion individual gas

35:46.860 --> 35:47.880
molecules inside.

35:47.880 --> 35:49.460
That's the fine-grained view.

35:50.040 --> 35:53.560
Or you could just measure the average temperature and pressure of the box.

35:53.920 --> 35:55.520
That is the coarse-grained view.

35:56.080 --> 36:01.620
You throw away the specific data of every single molecule and you integrate over them

36:01.620 --> 36:03.980
to get a simplified observable macro state.

36:04.140 --> 36:05.060
You just blur your eyes.

36:05.120 --> 36:05.720
You blur your eyes.

36:05.800 --> 36:05.960
Yeah.

36:06.320 --> 36:11.160
Brandes proved mathematically that quantum probability operates the exact same way.

36:11.800 --> 36:14.520
Probability isn't a fundamental building block of reality.

36:15.200 --> 36:16.780
Probability is an emergent property.

36:16.780 --> 36:22.000
It is what is left over after you integrate out or coarse-grained, the unobserved internal

36:22.000 --> 36:23.440
degrees of freedom of the universe.

36:23.880 --> 36:27.620
The Born rule is just the mathematical equivalent of blurring your eyes.

36:27.820 --> 36:28.260
Wow.

36:28.260 --> 36:34.280
So the universe has all this incredibly complex internal geometric data, the phases, rotations,

36:34.280 --> 36:36.520
and twistings in the admissibility manifold.

36:36.520 --> 36:41.860
And the Born rule, the act of squaring, is just the projection operator denoted by the Greek

36:41.860 --> 36:46.900
letter pi in the paper mapping that massive internal manifold down to our limited observable

36:46.900 --> 36:47.340
manifold.

36:47.820 --> 36:52.940
The Born rule is literally just the universe throwing away the internal geometric data so

36:52.940 --> 36:55.300
that we can comprehend it as a simple probability.

36:55.300 --> 36:58.140
That is exactly what the math implies.

36:58.640 --> 37:03.140
And when you apply this to our Crean space from earlier, the space with the ghosts, it solves

37:03.140 --> 37:04.080
the puzzle perfectly.

37:04.740 --> 37:08.800
The ghosts in the Crean space are associated with hyperbolic rotations in the geometry.

37:09.520 --> 37:13.920
When you apply the projection operator pi, the squaring operation of the Born rule structurally

37:13.920 --> 37:16.200
throws away those specific hyperbolic rotations.

37:16.200 --> 37:20.300
The ghosts are literally just geometric rotations that get discarded in the projection.

37:20.840 --> 37:21.620
They are squared away.

37:21.840 --> 37:26.380
I have a deep philosophical question about this then, because this is honestly unsettling.

37:27.100 --> 37:32.040
If the Born rule isn't fundamental, if it's just a coarse graining, a throwing away of

