The actual reality of the computer is billions of microscopic silicon transistors firing electrical

39:32.600 --> 39:34.540
voltages on and off inside the CPU.

39:35.440 --> 39:39.380
But you couldn't possibly comprehend or interact with a billion voltages a second.

39:39.380 --> 39:45.360
So the operating system projects a simplified, coarse-grained interface, a desktop, that allows

39:45.360 --> 39:47.780
you to interact with the underlying system efficiently.

39:48.380 --> 39:52.820
So you're saying Einstein's general relativity, the crowning achievement of 20th century physics,

39:53.100 --> 39:54.960
is just the desktop icon?

39:55.520 --> 39:56.760
In this framework, yes.

39:57.440 --> 39:59.320
General relativity is the first-order interface.

39:59.700 --> 40:02.460
It's the simplest, lowest-resolution description of the projection.

40:03.200 --> 40:07.340
Quadratic gravity-stellars theory with the extra-squared terms is the second-order interface.

40:07.340 --> 40:10.500
It's a slightly higher-resolution look at the underlying code.

40:10.920 --> 40:15.200
And spacetime curvature itself, the bending of space that we feel is gravity, is not a

40:15.200 --> 40:15.940
fundamental field.

40:16.360 --> 40:20.040
It is just the shadow of the projection pi feeling to be perfectly flat.

40:20.780 --> 40:25.240
Curvature is the physical manifestation of the geometric obstruction between the complex

40:25.240 --> 40:28.560
internal manifold and our limited observable reality.

40:28.840 --> 40:33.460
Okay, if this interface theory is true, what does this mean for string theory?

40:33.460 --> 40:39.160
Because physicists have spent half a century telling the public that to unite quantum mechanics

40:39.160 --> 40:45.780
