40:53.260 --> 40:57.720
This is where Turok's critique becomes utterly devastating to the orthodoxy.

40:58.440 --> 41:01.860
Why did string theory need 10 or 26 dimensions in the first place?

41:02.180 --> 41:04.600
Have you ever wondered why they picked those specific numbers?

41:04.840 --> 41:09.040
I mean, I always assumed it was just where the math naturally led them to solve gravity.

41:09.220 --> 41:11.720
It was where the math led them, because of the Hilbert assumption.

41:12.260 --> 41:16.240
When string theorists in the 70s and 80s tried to quantize the relativistic string,

41:16.620 --> 41:20.140
they found that mathematical anomalies, specifically the conformal anomaly,

41:20.140 --> 41:23.440
kept generating negative norm states, ghosts.

41:24.160 --> 41:28.060
The internal mathematical space was naturally trying to be a Kreen space.

41:28.200 --> 41:28.820
Oh, wow.

41:28.920 --> 41:29.180
Right.

41:29.480 --> 41:34.080
But because the physicists were philosophically terrified of negative probabilities,

41:34.600 --> 41:37.680
they demanded a mathematical trick to kill the ghosts.

41:38.180 --> 41:43.060
They discovered that if you artificially force the universe to have exactly 26 dimensions

41:43.060 --> 41:47.180
for bosonic strings, or exactly 10 dimensions if you add supersymmetry,

41:47.180 --> 41:53.180
the math perfectly cancels the conformal anomaly and completely deletes the negative norm states.

41:53.320 --> 41:53.840
Wait, wait, wait.

41:54.140 --> 41:55.560
Let me get this absolutely straight.

41:55.800 --> 41:59.940
Are you telling me we spent 50 years looking for 11 dimensions because we simply refused

41:59.940 --> 42:02.140
to let our math have negative numbers in the internal ledger?

42:02.280 --> 42:08.280
We built a massive, untestable theoretical multiverse just to satisfy a philosophical accounting preference.

42:08.700 --> 42:10.720
That is exactly what this paper is alleging.

42:10.720 --> 42:15.840
The entire foundational necessity of string theory was built on the absolute demand

42:15.840 --> 42:18.560
to maintain a stripped Hilbert space internally.

42:19.260 --> 42:23.680
If you drop the Hilbert assumption, if you allow the internal ledger to be a Kreen space

42:23.680 --> 42:26.840
and trust the projection operator to balance the books at the ATM,

42:27.280 --> 42:29.740
the necessity for extra dimensions simply vanishes.

42:30.580 --> 42:34.200
You no longer need 10 dimensions to make quantum gravity mathematically consistent.

42:34.640 --> 42:37.220
Quadratic gravity, acting as an interface theory,

42:37.220 --> 42:40.340
can do it in our standard observable four dimensions.

42:40.960 --> 42:41.440
But how?

42:41.720 --> 42:45.560
The whole point of string theory was to smear out the point-like nature of particles

42:45.560 --> 42:49.860
to stop the high-energy interactions from becoming infinitely strong at the Planck scale.

42:50.260 --> 42:55.080
How does quadratic gravity actually work in four dimensions without breaking down when you zoom in?

42:55.380 --> 42:57.760
Because of a property called asymptotic freedom.

42:58.420 --> 43:00.540
This is a well-understood phenomenon in physics.

43:01.200 --> 43:03.480
It behaves very much like the strong nuclear force,

43:03.660 --> 43:05.400
quantum chromodynamics, or QCD.

43:05.400 --> 43:10.840
In QCD, quarks are bound tightly together at low energies inside protons.

43:11.260 --> 43:13.540
If you try to pull them apart, the force gets stronger.

43:14.160 --> 43:16.600
But if you smash them together at ultra-high energies,

43:16.880 --> 43:18.420
the interaction actually gets weaker.

43:18.860 --> 43:19.760
The force shuts down.

43:20.220 --> 43:21.740
The particles act as if they are free.

43:22.240 --> 43:25.240
This is asymptotic freedom, and it won a Nobel Prize.

43:25.400 --> 43:26.900
Okay, and gravity does this.

43:27.200 --> 43:30.300
A mathematician named Avramidi proved in the 1980s

43:30.300 --> 43:33.020
that quadratic gravity has this exact same property.

43:33.020 --> 43:35.740
At everyday energies, gravity is attractive.

43:36.340 --> 43:39.240
But at ultra-high energies, as you approach the Planck scale,

43:39.660 --> 43:42.120
the realm of the Big Bang or the center of a black hole,

43:42.600 --> 43:44.440
the gravitational interactions fade away.

43:45.000 --> 43:47.220
The theory becomes arbitrarily weakly coupled.

43:47.760 --> 43:51.740
It becomes UV-complete, meaning mathematically safe at the highest possible energies,

43:52.120 --> 43:53.180
in just four dimensions.

43:53.720 --> 43:56.120
It doesn't need strings to smear out the infinities,

43:56.120 --> 43:58.480
because the force itself dynamically shuts down.

43:58.900 --> 43:59.640
That is staggering.

44:00.080 --> 44:04.300
