49:38.780 --> 49:40.480
They are plagued by coordinate ghosts.

49:41.040 --> 49:42.080
But they also possess

49:42.080 --> 49:44.860
a massive, infinite-dimensional gauge symmetry

49:44.860 --> 49:47.580
that allows you to mathematically shift the field

49:47.580 --> 49:49.280
by any harmonic function.

49:49.900 --> 49:52.120
When you rigorously account for this symmetry,

49:52.540 --> 49:53.500
you find that the theory

49:53.500 --> 49:55.720
has no local degrees of freedom at all.

49:56.460 --> 49:58.040
The projection operator pi

49:58.040 --> 50:00.760
maps the entire complex admissibility manifold

50:00.760 --> 50:03.640
down to a single, unique physical state

50:03.640 --> 50:05.140
in the observable manifold,

50:05.140 --> 50:06.260
the vacuum.

50:06.780 --> 50:08.980
So the entire chaotic internal field of ghosts

50:08.980 --> 50:10.600
perfectly cancels itself out

50:10.600 --> 50:12.360
to leave behind absolute nothingness,

50:12.480 --> 50:13.720
a perfectly stable vacuum.

50:14.360 --> 50:15.660
Why introduce them at all

50:15.660 --> 50:16.420
if they just vanish?

50:16.520 --> 50:17.900
What problem do they actually solve

50:17.900 --> 50:18.420
in the background?

50:18.640 --> 50:20.020
They solve the Weill anomaly.

50:20.660 --> 50:21.960
When you take the standard model

50:21.960 --> 50:22.980
of particle physics,

50:23.220 --> 50:24.680
quarks, electrons, photons,

50:24.940 --> 50:26.060
and you put them in a

50:26.060 --> 50:27.500
curved space-time background,

50:27.780 --> 50:29.560
like a galaxy or the expanding universe,

50:29.960 --> 50:31.820
the quantum fluctuations of those particles

50:31.820 --> 50:32.640
produce an anomaly.

50:33.280 --> 50:34.920
Specifically, the trace of the stress

50:34.920 --> 50:36.680
energy tensor no longer equals zero.

50:37.200 --> 50:38.500
This breaks conformal symmetry,

50:38.720 --> 50:40.000
which is a mathematical disaster

50:40.000 --> 50:41.620
for theories that rely on scale

50:41.620 --> 50:42.920
and variance at the Big Bang.

50:43.340 --> 50:44.540
And how did physicists try

50:44.540 --> 50:45.840
to fix this anomaly before?

50:46.380 --> 50:47.920
Historically, physicists thought

50:47.920 --> 50:49.460
the only way to cancel this anomaly

50:49.460 --> 50:51.320
was to invent supersymmetry.

50:52.000 --> 50:53.940
They theorized a whole suite

50:53.940 --> 50:55.900
of undiscovered mirror particles,

50:56.600 --> 50:58.680
selectrons, squarks, neutrolinos,

50:59.080 --> 51:00.260
whose quantum fluctuations

51:00.260 --> 51:01.720
would perfectly cancel out

51:01.720 --> 51:03.380
the standard model fluctuations.

51:03.380 --> 51:05.040
Which is very convenient,

51:05.200 --> 51:06.720
since the Large Hadron Collider

51:06.720 --> 51:07.980
has spent over a decade

51:07.980 --> 51:09.220
and billions of dollars

51:09.220 --> 51:10.700
smashing protons together

51:10.700 --> 51:12.040
looking for supersymmetry

51:12.040 --> 51:14.100
and hasn't found a single shred

51:14.100 --> 51:15.320
of evidence that it actually

51:15.320 --> 51:16.160
exists in nature.

51:16.580 --> 51:17.140
Precisely.

51:17.740 --> 51:19.060
Supersymmetry is a ghost town

51:19.060 --> 51:19.560
of colliders.

51:20.220 --> 51:21.440
But Boyle and Turok

51:21.440 --> 51:22.340
showed mathematically

51:22.340 --> 51:23.880
that you don't need millions

51:23.880 --> 51:24.940
of undiscovered

51:24.940 --> 51:25.980
supersymmetric particles.

51:26.620 --> 51:28.220
These strange, invisible

51:28.220 --> 51:29.680
dimension zero scalars

51:29.680 --> 51:30.640
contribute negatively

51:30.640 --> 51:31.800
to the anomaly coefficients.

51:32.600 --> 51:33.540
They act as the perfect

51:33.540 --> 51:34.600
mathematical counterweight.

51:35.000 --> 51:35.940
They perfectly cancel

51:35.940 --> 51:36.740
the Boyle anomaly

51:36.740 --> 51:37.640
without needing

51:37.640 --> 51:39.160
a single new physical particle.

51:39.400 --> 51:40.700
Okay, that is clever math.

51:40.780 --> 51:41.760
But here's where

51:41.760 --> 51:42.660
I'm going to push back again

51:42.660 --> 51:43.460
because the paper makes

51:43.460 --> 51:44.560
a jaw-dropping claim

51:44.560 --> 51:46.360
about predicting the exact number

51:46.360 --> 51:47.560
of particles in the universe.

51:48.060 --> 51:49.400
It says the math demands

51:49.400 --> 51:50.900
exactly three generations

51:50.900 --> 51:52.600
of standard model fermions.

51:52.740 --> 51:53.280
So an electron,

51:53.540 --> 51:54.600
a muon, and a tau.

51:54.880 --> 51:56.220
That's three generations.

51:56.220 --> 51:58.740
And we happen to actually have

51:58.740 --> 52:00.040
exactly three generations

52:00.040 --> 52:01.340
of matter in reality.

52:02.080 --> 52:03.620
But whenever a theoretical physicist

52:03.620 --> 52:04.820
tells me their new model

52:04.820 --> 52:05.820
perfectly predicts

52:05.820 --> 52:06.960
a number we already knew,

52:07.140 --> 52:08.360
I immediately get suspicious.

52:08.840 --> 52:10.060
That's called post-addiction.

52:10.940 --> 52:11.960
Did Boyle and Turok

52:11.960 --> 52:13.460
just manually tune the dials

52:13.460 --> 52:14.700
of their dimension zero fields

52:14.700 --> 52:16.260
until the math magically spit out

52:16.260 --> 52:17.280
48 fermions

52:17.280 --> 52:18.500
just to match the textbook?

52:18.760 --> 52:20.060
That is the standard,

52:20.400 --> 52:21.160
highly warranted

52:21.160 --> 52:22.160
skeptical response.

52:22.800 --> 52:23.660
But here's why

52:23.660 --> 52:24.560
this is so profound.

52:24.560 --> 52:26.780
There are no dials to tune.

52:27.420 --> 52:29.140
In order for the dimension zero scalars

52:29.140 --> 52:29.860
to leave behind

52:29.860 --> 52:31.160
a perfectly stable vacuum,

52:31.640 --> 52:32.700
their gauge symmetries

52:32.700 --> 52:34.300
must be mathematically exact.

52:34.980 --> 52:35.980
And for the vacuum energy

52:35.980 --> 52:37.040
and the whale anomaly

52:37.040 --> 52:38.720
to perfectly cancel out to zero

52:38.720 --> 52:39.960
at the origin of the universe,

52:40.440 --> 52:41.700
the topological requirements

52:41.700 --> 52:42.340
of the mathematics

52:42.340 --> 52:43.560
are incredibly rigid.

52:44.000 --> 52:45.260
The coefficients of the anomaly

52:45.260 --> 52:46.160
are determined strictly

52:46.160 --> 52:46.820
by the spin

52:46.820 --> 52:48.320
and number of the fields involved.

52:48.800 --> 52:50.220
It is an algebraic lock.

52:50.960 --> 52:52.040
When you set the equations

52:52.040 --> 52:54.260
to demand total anomaly cancellation,

52:54.560 --> 52:56.020
the algebra spits out

52:56.020 --> 52:56.880
a strict requirement.

52:57.400 --> 52:58.340
The universe must contain

52:58.340 --> 52:59.660
exactly three generations

52:59.660 --> 53:01.260
of standard model fermions.

53:01.540 --> 53:02.340
Meaning if there were

53:02.340 --> 53:03.320
four generations

53:03.320 --> 53:04.440
or two generations,

53:04.760 --> 53:05.960
the anomaly wouldn't cancel,

53:06.180 --> 53:07.260
the interface would fail,

53:07.380 --> 53:08.600
and the universe wouldn't exist.

53:08.860 --> 53:09.360
It's exactly.

53:09.580 --> 53:10.100
For decades,

53:10.200 --> 53:10.960
the standard model

53:10.960 --> 53:12.460
has had these three generations

53:12.460 --> 53:14.600
making 48 fermions in total.

53:15.260 --> 53:17.520
And physicists have agonizingly wondered

53:17.520 --> 53:18.300
why there are three.

53:18.800 --> 53:20.020
Who ordered the muon?

53:20.460 --> 53:21.240
Why does the matter

53:21.240 --> 53:22.400
repeat itself three times

53:22.400 --> 53:23.320
and then abruptly stop?

53:23.720 --> 53:24.520
In the standard model,

53:24.640 --> 53:26.460
it's just an arbitrary parameter,

53:26.740 --> 53:27.280
an accident.

53:27.840 --> 53:29.320
But in the Boyle-Torok model,

53:29.800 --> 53:30.580
it isn't arbitrary.

53:31.180 --> 53:32.760
The theory genuinely predicts

53:32.760 --> 53:33.800
the structure of matter

53:33.800 --> 53:35.020
because anything else

53:35.020 --> 53:35.940
would fail to cancel

53:35.940 --> 53:37.340
the gravitational anomalies

53:37.340 --> 53:38.720
of the invisibility manifold.

53:39.180 --> 53:39.580
That is...

53:39.580 --> 53:39.880
Wow.

53:40.060 --> 53:40.940
I concede the point.

53:41.140 --> 53:42.080
That isn't dial tuning.

53:42.240 --> 53:43.080
That is discovering

53:43.080 --> 53:44.000
structural architecture.

53:44.440 --> 53:45.060
It's like finding

53:45.060 --> 53:46.500
a mysterious gear in a clock

53:46.500 --> 53:47.760
and then discovering that

53:47.760 --> 53:49.760
if that gear had one fewer tooth,

53:49.760 --> 53:51.200
the whole clock would shatter.

53:51.440 --> 53:53.280
It predicts the exact structure of matter,

53:53.380 --> 53:54.340
but it goes even further, right?

53:54.700 --> 53:56.340
Let's talk about the Big Bang itself.

53:56.700 --> 53:57.620
The paper discusses

53:57.620 --> 53:59.100
the CPT symmetric universe.

53:59.220 --> 54:00.260
What does CPT mean?

54:00.580 --> 54:02.000
CPT is an acronym

54:02.000 --> 54:03.180
for charge conjugation,

54:03.700 --> 54:04.300
parity inversion,

54:04.480 --> 54:05.080
and time reversal.

54:05.500 --> 54:07.140
It is the most fundamental symmetry

54:07.140 --> 54:08.580
in all of quantum mechanics.

54:09.380 --> 54:10.560
Charge conjugation swaps

54:10.560 --> 54:11.760
matter with antimatter.

54:12.360 --> 54:14.140
Parity inversion flips left and right

54:14.140 --> 54:14.720
like a mirror.

54:15.400 --> 54:16.280
Time reversal runs

54:16.280 --> 54:17.000
the clock backward.

54:17.620 --> 54:19.040
The CPT theorem dictates

54:19.040 --> 54:20.540
that if you take any physical system,

54:21.020 --> 54:21.720
flip its charge,

54:21.960 --> 54:22.700
flip it in a mirror,

54:22.800 --> 54:23.860
or run it backward in time,

54:24.060 --> 54:24.740
it must obey

54:24.740 --> 54:26.400
the exact same laws of physics.

54:26.740 --> 54:27.020
Okay.

54:27.280 --> 54:28.060
But what does that have to do

54:28.060 --> 54:28.740
with the Big Bang?

54:29.040 --> 54:30.200
In standard cosmology,

54:30.560 --> 54:32.280
the Big Bang is a singularity,

54:32.500 --> 54:33.300
an edge of time

54:33.300 --> 54:35.020
where physics completely breaks down.

54:35.600 --> 54:37.160
And standard cosmology assumes

54:37.160 --> 54:38.340
that the universe spontaneously

54:38.340 --> 54:39.520
violated symmetries

54:39.520 --> 54:40.180
as it expanded.

54:40.880 --> 54:42.360
But physicists Latham Boyle,

54:42.700 --> 54:43.320
Karen Finn,

54:43.320 --> 54:44.400
and Neil Turok

54:44.400 --> 54:46.320
proposed a radical alternative.

54:47.000 --> 54:47.780
What if the universe

54:47.780 --> 54:49.360
does not spontaneously violate

54:49.360 --> 54:50.460
CPT of the Big Bang?

54:50.840 --> 54:51.520
What if the universe

54:51.520 --> 54:52.520
after the Big Bang

54:52.520 --> 54:54.240
is the exact mathematical

54:54.240 --> 54:55.540
CPT mirror image

54:55.540 --> 54:56.120
of a universe

54:56.120 --> 54:57.080
before the Big Bang?

54:57.200 --> 54:57.600
So,

54:58.120 --> 54:59.320
if time is flowing forward

54:59.320 --> 55:00.200
for us right now,

55:00.680 --> 55:01.640
expanding out of

55:01.640 --> 55:02.960
the Big Bang singularity,

55:03.300 --> 55:03.880
you are saying

55:03.880 --> 55:05.180
there is a mirror universe

55:05.180 --> 55:06.560
on the other side

55:06.560 --> 55:07.400
of the singularity

55:07.400 --> 55:08.940
where time is flowing backward,

55:09.220 --> 55:09.940
expanding away

55:09.940 --> 55:12.180
in the opposite temporal direction,

55:12.180 --> 55:14.160
like a reflection in a pond.

55:14.160 --> 55:14.660
Yes,

55:14.860 --> 55:15.820
an anti-universe

55:15.820 --> 55:17.440
emerging from the exact

55:17.440 --> 55:18.940
same conformal singularity.

55:19.320 --> 55:19.880
It's an elegant,

55:20.220 --> 55:21.440
perfectly symmetric geometry.

55:22.100 --> 55:23.180
But this isn't just

55:23.180 --> 55:23.960
science fiction

55:23.960 --> 55:25.040
or philosophical poetry.

55:25.600 --> 55:26.680
Demanding this perfect

55:26.680 --> 55:27.840
CPT symmetry

55:27.840 --> 55:28.880
across the Big Bang

55:28.880 --> 55:30.640
has incredibly rigorous

55:30.640 --> 55:31.780
mathematical consequences

55:31.780 --> 55:32.880
for our side of the mirror.

55:33.140 --> 55:34.740
By enforcing this symmetry,

55:35.080 --> 55:36.360
you drastically restrict

55:36.360 --> 55:37.760
the possible boundary conditions

55:37.760 --> 55:38.460
of the universe.

55:38.840 --> 55:39.940
It naturally selects

55:39.940 --> 55:40.400
a unique,

55:40.580 --> 55:41.880
preferred vacuum state.

55:41.880 --> 55:43.180
And when you calculate

55:43.180 --> 55:44.060
the thermodynamics

55:44.060 --> 55:45.560
of that specific vacuum state

55:45.560 --> 55:46.340
expanding outward,

55:46.900 --> 55:48.280
the math naturally produces

55:48.280 --> 55:50.060
a stable right-handed neutrino.

55:50.220 --> 55:51.200
A right-handed neutrino.

55:51.280 --> 55:51.940
I know neutrinos

55:51.940 --> 55:52.740
are the ghost particles

55:52.740 --> 55:53.540
of the standard model.

55:53.640 --> 55:54.400
They barely interact

55:54.400 --> 55:54.880
with anything.

55:55.140 --> 55:55.800
What is special

55:55.800 --> 55:56.760
about a right-handed one?

55:57.000 --> 55:57.740
All neutrinos

55:57.740 --> 55:58.560
we have ever observed

55:58.560 --> 55:59.920
in nature are left-handed,

56:00.420 --> 56:01.840
referring to their quantum spin

56:01.840 --> 56:02.980
relative to their momentum.

56:03.540 --> 56:04.440
But the math

56:04.440 --> 56:05.360
of the standard model

56:05.360 --> 56:06.560
strongly implies

56:06.560 --> 56:08.340
that right-handed mirror versions

56:08.340 --> 56:09.120
should exist.

56:09.920 --> 56:11.320
They just haven't been seen

56:11.320 --> 56:12.600
because they only interact

56:12.600 --> 56:13.180
via gravity.

56:13.320 --> 56:13.820
They don't feel

56:13.820 --> 56:15.140
the weak nuclear force.

56:16.000 --> 56:17.960
In this CPT-symmetric model,

56:18.480 --> 56:19.680
the Big Bang pumps out

56:19.680 --> 56:20.840
a massive population

56:20.840 --> 56:22.180
of these right-handed neutrinos.

56:22.340 --> 56:23.160
And what happens to them?

56:23.360 --> 56:24.100
They just sit there.

56:24.440 --> 56:25.500
Because they only interact

56:25.500 --> 56:26.220
via gravity,

56:26.340 --> 56:27.500
they're incredibly stable.

56:28.060 --> 56:29.220
And when Boyle and Turok

56:29.220 --> 56:31.000
calculated the precise density

56:31.000 --> 56:32.480
of these right-handed neutrinos

56:32.480 --> 56:33.660
produced by the Big Bang

56:33.660 --> 56:35.500
in this CPT-symmetric model,

56:35.980 --> 56:37.040
they found something astonishing.

56:37.900 --> 56:38.840
If you assume

56:38.840 --> 56:40.320
one of these right-handed neutrinos

56:40.320 --> 56:40.860
is stable,

56:41.320 --> 56:42.220
the math requires it

56:42.220 --> 56:42.940
to have a mass

56:42.940 --> 56:46.280
of approximately 4.8 times 10 to the 8th g.

56:46.980 --> 56:48.200
And when you plug that mass

56:48.200 --> 56:49.540
into the density equations

56:49.540 --> 56:50.680
of the universe...

56:50.680 --> 56:51.260
Let me guess.

56:51.540 --> 56:52.560
It perfectly matches

56:52.560 --> 56:53.740
the observed density

56:53.740 --> 56:54.460
of dark matter.

56:54.860 --> 56:56.060
It matches it perfectly.

56:56.860 --> 56:57.620
Dark matter isn't

56:57.620 --> 56:59.800
some exotic new fundamental force

56:59.800 --> 57:01.220
or weakly interacting

57:01.220 --> 57:02.160
massive particle

57:02.160 --> 57:04.020
that requires entirely new physics

57:04.020 --> 57:05.320
or a halo

57:05.320 --> 57:06.840
of microscopic black holes.

57:06.840 --> 57:08.520
It is simply a heady

57:08.520 --> 57:09.840
right-handed neutrino

57:09.840 --> 57:11.260
that was naturally produced

57:11.260 --> 57:12.680
by the perfect mirror symmetry

57:12.680 --> 57:13.500
of the Big Bang.

57:13.500 --> 57:14.900
You've got to be kidding me.

57:15.060 --> 57:16.220
We have spent billions

57:16.220 --> 57:17.580
on underground vats

57:17.580 --> 57:18.520
of liquid xenon

57:18.520 --> 57:19.500
trying to detect

57:19.500 --> 57:20.780
dark matter wimps

57:20.780 --> 57:22.020
and this theory says

57:22.020 --> 57:23.020
it's just a neutrino

57:23.020 --> 57:23.880
falling out of a mirror.

57:24.240 --> 57:25.580
That is the strict prediction.

57:25.980 --> 57:27.220
No ad hoc parameters,

57:27.420 --> 57:28.180
no fine-tuning,

57:28.380 --> 57:29.680
no invisible dark sectors.

57:29.840 --> 57:31.500
It just mathematically drops

57:31.500 --> 57:32.720
out of the thermodynamics

57:32.720 --> 57:34.340
of a CPT-symmetric universe.

57:35.140 --> 57:35.780
And furthermore,

57:35.860 --> 57:37.080
this same exact model

57:37.080 --> 57:38.480
predicts the precise pattern

57:38.480 --> 57:39.400
of ripples we see

57:39.400 --> 57:40.240
in the oldest light

57:40.240 --> 57:40.840
in the universe,

57:41.260 --> 57:42.560
the cosmic microwave background.

57:42.560 --> 57:43.180
How so?

57:43.540 --> 57:44.400
It predicts what are called

57:44.400 --> 57:45.340
Harrison-Zeldovich

57:45.340 --> 57:46.200
scale-invariant

57:46.200 --> 57:47.840
primordial density perturbations.

57:48.280 --> 57:49.720
It calculates a specific value

57:49.720 --> 57:50.640
for the spectral index

57:50.640 --> 57:51.200
of these ripples

57:51.200 --> 57:53.020
designated as n-subs.

57:53.440 --> 57:54.080
The theory predicts

57:54.080 --> 57:54.940
n-sub-s should be

57:54.940 --> 57:56.320
roughly 0.958.

57:56.660 --> 57:57.840
And what does the actual

57:57.840 --> 57:58.660
observational data

57:58.660 --> 58:00.400
from our most advanced satellites

58:00.400 --> 58:01.420
like the Planck satellite

58:01.420 --> 58:03.160
say the index actually is?

58:03.320 --> 58:04.220
The Planck data

58:04.220 --> 58:06.240
measures it at 0.959

58:06.240 --> 58:09.180
plus or minus 0.006.

58:09.520 --> 58:11.260
It is a stunningly perfect

58:11.260 --> 58:12.160
match with the data.

58:12.160 --> 58:14.060
And here is the coup de grace.

58:14.900 --> 58:16.340
The CPT-symmetric model

58:16.340 --> 58:17.460
specifically predicts

58:17.460 --> 58:17.920
the existence

58:17.920 --> 58:19.260
of zero primordial

58:19.260 --> 58:20.320
gravitational waves.

58:20.980 --> 58:22.260
The tensor-to-scalar ratio

58:22.260 --> 58:22.960
known as R

58:22.960 --> 58:24.180
is strictly zero.

58:24.420 --> 58:25.180
Why does that matter?

58:25.400 --> 58:26.840
Because it entirely eliminates

58:26.840 --> 58:28.160
the need for cosmic inflation.

58:28.380 --> 58:29.380
Cosmic inflation.

58:30.260 --> 58:31.220
The prevailing theory

58:31.220 --> 58:31.880
that the universe

58:31.880 --> 58:32.700
expanded faster

58:32.700 --> 58:33.560
than the speed of light

58:33.560 --> 58:34.400
in the first fraction

58:34.400 --> 58:34.900
of a second

58:34.900 --> 58:36.200
to smooth everything out

58:36.200 --> 58:37.140
and seed those ripples.

58:37.600 --> 58:38.520
This model says

58:38.520 --> 58:39.140
we don't need

58:39.140 --> 58:40.020
the most famous

58:40.020 --> 58:41.180
cosmological theory

58:41.180 --> 58:42.320
of the last 40 years.

58:42.440 --> 58:43.040
It says inflation

58:43.040 --> 58:43.780
is an entirely

58:43.780 --> 58:45.460
unnecessary ad hoc addition.

58:46.120 --> 58:46.620
You don't need

58:46.620 --> 58:48.060
a magical inflightened field

58:48.060 --> 58:49.280
to smooth out the universe.

58:49.940 --> 58:51.180
The scale-invariant ripples

58:51.180 --> 58:52.260
are naturally generated

58:52.260 --> 58:53.540
by the conformal behavior

58:53.540 --> 58:55.020
of those dimension zero scalars

58:55.020 --> 58:55.700
we talked about.

58:56.100 --> 58:57.200
And the large-scale

58:57.200 --> 58:58.280
smoothness of the universe

58:58.280 --> 58:59.400
is just the natural

58:59.400 --> 59:00.740
